==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Magical Cat☆ Magica''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Similarly to the [[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|ULTRA SOULS]], Madoka Cat & Homura has significantly different stats between Normal (spammable) and Evolved Form (high performance), both of which can be used effectively depending on the situation.

==='''Normal Form'''===
Madoka Cat & Homura are not great to put it lightly. She can be directly compared to [[Fortune Teller Cat (Rare Cat)|Doctor Cat]], exchanging spammability, attack rate, and movement speed for damage, health, and an additional [[Curse]] ability. Even with these upgrades in survivability and damage, she struggles to stay on the field long enough to make any of them count. Due to the dubious nature of the [[Knockback]] ability, she also struggles to find proper applicability, even if the stars align to give her a chance to activate it. These abysmal stats and abilities result in an even worse unit that is outclassed by more consistent units with more relevant abilities like [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]], [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]], and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]].

Even so, she was given one final ace up her sleeve: a [[Surge Attack#Mini-Surge|Mini-Surge]] ability with a 40% proc rate. This dramatically increases her DPS by a jaw-dropping... 8% on average, and grants her the capability of hitting enemies beyond her range (with a ~50% chance for it to inflict either of her two debuffs). The miniscule chance her Mini-Surge even lands on an enemy is further compounded by the mediocre odds it even carries one of her abilities. The likelihood these effects ever contribute positively to a battle are not worth considering in a practical sense. To add further insult to injury, she's also outclassed in her role of sniping Alien backliners by [[Ancient Egg: N105 (Rare Cat)|Racquet Cat]], who has higher range, more health, and a 30% knockback chance.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Magical Cat☆ Magica is an interesting unit, being a [[Grand Chunchun Haunters]] variant that targets Floating and Alien enemies. One of its traits is an upgrade over the original variant: targeting Aliens gives Magical Cat☆ Magica the opportunity to inflict Curse and Knockback on some of the most ability‐reliant enemy types. Notable targets include [[Maawth]]'s Freeze and [[Nimoy Bore]]'s Knockback, with Starred Aliens like [[Star Peng]], in particular, having their [[Warp]] ability disabled.

In practice, however, these two abilities have hardly any synergy. Knockback (especially) tends to draw out the battle and make other units whiff attacks as well. This occasionally works to the unit's detriment; for example, with [[Axoloty]], [[Calamary]], or [[Corporal Weyland]], which allows these enemies to reposition when hit. Moreover, Magical Cat☆ Magica's awful damage prevents it from playing much of an attacking role against such enemies either. Therefore, this unit should seldom be used to handle midrangers or backliners of its traits; instead, it is best suited for frontline support against enemies such as [[Bun Bun Symbiote]], Nimoy Bore, [[LeMurr]], etc. In this role, it can continously stop the advance of pesky Aliens/Floating enemies, especially with its quick attack rate.

Against Floating enemies specifically, the unit sees little application outside of crowd‐controlling [[Teacher Bun Bun]] variants and Cyclones. However, its [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]] allows it to act as a counter to [[Pigeon de Sable]] and enables its use in stages featuring the [[Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Doge Base]]. Additionally, Mini-Surge should be considered a bonus, as its spawn radius is far too inconsistent to be used effectively under any circumstances—even though it does allow Magical Cat☆ Magica to snipe enemies beyond its standing range.

Finally, '''note that this unit does not have [[Witch Killer]]'''. Consequently, Magical Cat☆ Magica is completely ineffective against enemies from its [[Puella Magi Madoka Magica Collaboration Event|Collaboration Event]].

